# ── Participant data and HPC staging ──────────────────────────────────────────
# Per-subject task CSVs contain individual participant data and are never
# committed.  They are regenerated locally by hgf_pipeline.py.
data/
data_n_cmnds/

# Out-of-set normative cohort: trial-level data belongs to a separate study and
# is not redistributed here.  The column dictionary and all derived summary
# CSVs/figures ARE tracked.
out_of_set_data/behavioral_data_OUT_OF_SET_with_metadata.csv

# ── HGF fit results (HPC outputs; large, auto-generated) ──────────────────────
/results/

# ── Model comparison outputs (auto-generated) ─────────────────────────────────
model_comparison/bms/results/
model_comparison/bms/lme_per_subject.csv
model_comparison/figures/

# bms_summary.csv is TRACKED, unlike the rest of this block: it is a 4-row
# aggregate (model, alpha, Ef, XP, PXP, BOR, n) with no participant-level data,
# and 04_visualizations/supplement/hgf_bms_modified.py reads it to render the
# RFX-BMS supplementary panel.  Without it that figure, and panel c of the
# 6-panel HGF validation figure, cannot be produced from a fresh clone.
!model_comparison/bms/bms_summary.csv

